  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A deviation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> is produced in the yellow ray when prism of crown and flint glass are achromatically combined. Taking dispersive powers of crown and flint glass are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></math>&nbsp;respectively and refractive index for yellow light for these glasses are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math> respectively. The refracting angles for crown glass prism will be ________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#176;</mo></math> (in degree)</p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "12",
